      "text": "A connected component of a topological space X is a nonempty connected subset of X that is maximal under inclusion among connected subsets of X.",
      "reason": "Stacks §5.7 explicitly requires connected spaces/subsets to be nonempty. Under mathDef's broader no-separation meaning the empty subset is connected, so make nonemptiness explicit to preserve the Stacks maximal-subset component definition when X is empty.",
